  "details": "I've been switching back and forth between playing this game on my Valve Index and desktop. A few days ago while on VRChat while on the Index, the audio was working fine. I've recently gone back to the game while in Non-VR mode and on desktop; the game seems to acknowledge that it's detecting my voice but no one can hear me for some reason.\nI've made sure that the game's default mic settings are not the Valve Index mic and I've set it back to my USB headset for general voice chatting. I thought it was my ping at first, and I've run all the voice settings to max 100% but nobody can still hear me.\nI haven't tried using the Valve Index again but I'd like to know if anyone's experienced this? I've reset the game, I've tinkered with the sound mixer on my Windows 10. Headset for general PC works for Discord and PS4, but not VRChat anymore for some reason.",
